                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2cac6a52-915b-3ee7-8f9f-38e4ce52fa95",
                        "entry_id": "78935379-7b43-33b7-821c-7dc749fabef0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having the quality of entering into composition; compounded."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "67d5f6b6-708a-48c0-b7ae-efc854504a2a",
                                "sense_id": "2cac6a52-915b-3ee7-8f9f-38e4ce52fa95",
                                "text": "The compositive imagination is thus characterized for Avicenna by its power “to combine and separate parts of sensible objects with other parts.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6dbb1fff-087b-418f-867b-0633fefe0388",
                                "sense_id": "2cac6a52-915b-3ee7-8f9f-38e4ce52fa95",
                                "text": "As a common example, nouns and adjective ending with nen normally have a compositive form ending with s instead of nen. For example, ihminen (human being) has the compositive form ihmis, appearing in words like ihmiskunta (mankind) and ihmissuhde (personal relationship)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "808982a7-3113-389d-9947-752a6729ba23",
                        "entry_id": "78935379-7b43-33b7-821c-7dc749fabef0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Characterized by forming an understanding through the accumulation or combination of details, as opposed to deduction from a theoretical model."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "da6874bc-f165-4618-8fbb-e388f5d656e6",
                                "sense_id": "808982a7-3113-389d-9947-752a6729ba23",
                                "text": "A compositive rational mode is had in this way when we reason from causes to effects; the resolutive rational mode is in the opposite direction, from effects to causes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ce48dce-bd1b-429f-a911-af2750f21832",
                                "sense_id": "808982a7-3113-389d-9947-752a6729ba23",
                                "text": "From simple features of mental life familiar to us all, compositive theory infers more complex social phenomena in very general terms"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
